WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.990
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:08.746
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.046 --> 00:00:16.926
Unit thirty-three: Question Tags (all forms). Today you will check information with tags like isn't it? and don't you?.

4
00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:19.762
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.014
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.909
Isn't it?.

7
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:30.544
Isn't it? means a tag after a positive sentence with is.

8
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.337
It's cold, isn't it?

9
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.602
Your turn. Say: Isn't it?.

10
00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.375
Isn't it?.

11
00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:40.909
Don't you?.

12
00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:46.102
Don't you? means a tag after a positive present simple sentence.

13
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:48.310
You like tea, don't you?

14
00:00:48.917 --> 00:00:51.650
Your turn. Say: Don't you?.

15
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.397
Don't you?.

16
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:56.954
Can't she?.

17
00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.729
Can't she? means a tag after a positive can sentence.

18
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:04.049
She can swim, can't she?

19
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.500
Your turn. Say: Can't she?.

20
00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:11.172
Can't she?.

21
00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:12.871
Won't they?.

22
00:01:13.883 --> 00:01:17.523
Won't they? means a tag after a positive will sentence.

23
00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:19.512
They will come, won't they?

24
00:01:20.117 --> 00:01:22.548
Your turn. Say: Won't they?.

25
00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:26.297
Won't they?.

26
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.190
Shall we?.

27
00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.905
Shall we? means the tag after Let's.

28
00:01:32.517 --> 00:01:34.063
Let's go, shall we?

29
00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.105
Your turn. Say: Shall we?.

30
00:01:39.967 --> 00:01:40.782
Shall we?.

31
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:42.599
Aren't I?.

32
00:01:43.583 --> 00:01:46.619
Aren't I? means the special tag after I am.

33
00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:48.566
I'm late, aren't I?

34
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.325
Your turn. Say: Aren't I?.

35
00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.075
Aren't I?.

36
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:57.748
Let's.

37
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:00.854
Let's means a suggestion for us.

38
00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.625
Let's start.

39
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:05.428
Your turn. Say: Let's.

40
00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:09.233
Let's.

41
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:11.333
Rising voice.

42
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:15.663
Rising voice means a rising tone shows a real question.

43
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.448
The voice goes up.

44
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.749
Your turn. Say: Rising voice.

45
00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.042
Rising voice.

46
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:29.902
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.318
Visal, make a sentence with a question tag.

48
00:02:34.417 --> 00:02:43.480
It's a lovely day, isn't it? A question tag is a short question at the end of a statement. It checks information or asks for agreement.

49
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:45.759
What is the rule?

50
00:02:46.850 --> 00:03:02.792
Positive sentence, negative tag. Negative sentence, positive tag. You like tea, don't you? She isn't here, is she? The tag uses the same auxiliary as the sentence, and do for present or past simple.

51
00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.604
What are the special cases?

52
00:03:06.717 --> 00:03:17.724
I am becomes aren't I. Let's becomes shall we. An imperative takes will you. A rising voice means a real question. A falling voice means I expect you to agree.

53
00:03:18.867 --> 00:03:20.309
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:26.865
Grammar focus: Question tags: positive to negative, negative to positive.

55
00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:28.386
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:30.920
It's a lovely day, isn't it?

57
00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:33.340
You like tea, don't you?

58
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.820
I'm late, aren't I?

59
00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:46.701
Positive sentence + negative tag; negative sentence + positive tag. Use the same auxiliary (do for simple tenses). Special: aren't I, shall we.

60
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.031
Be careful! Don't say: You like tea, aren't you?

61
00:03:52.967 --> 00:03:55.222
Say: You like tea, don't you?

62
00:03:55.522 --> 00:03:57.382
Use the matching auxiliary.

63
00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.947
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:01.733 --> 00:04:02.618
Isn't It?.

65
00:04:02.918 --> 00:04:04.755
It's a lovely day, isn't it?

66
00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.360
You like tea, don't you?

67
00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.447
She can't swim, can she?

68
00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:13.479
Let's go to the market, shall we?

69
00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:17.244
With a rising voice, a tag is a real question.

70
00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:22.045
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:22.883 --> 00:04:24.279
She is a teacher, blank?

72
00:04:24.579 --> 00:04:28.395
A, isn't she. B, doesn't she. C, is she.

73
00:04:31.933 --> 00:04:33.828
The answer is A: isn't she.

74
00:04:34.983 --> 00:04:36.275
They didn't come, blank?

75
00:04:36.575 --> 00:04:40.042
A, didn't they. B, did they. C, do they.

76
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:45.623
The answer is B: did they.

77
00:04:46.783 --> 00:04:48.110
I'm late, blank?

78
00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:52.098
A, amn't I. B, aren't I. C, isn't I.

79
00:04:55.633 --> 00:04:57.679
The answer is B: aren't I.

80
00:04:58.817 --> 00:05:00.212
Let's go, blank?

81
00:05:00.512 --> 00:05:03.876
A, shall we. B, will we. C, don't we.

82
00:05:07.433 --> 00:05:09.421
The answer is A: shall we.

83
00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:12.769
According to the reading, where do they go?

84
00:05:13.069 --> 00:05:16.710
A, the market. B, the school. C, the park.

85
00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:22.220
The answer is A: the market.

86
00:05:23.433 --> 00:05:26.991
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.999
Write three sentences with different question tags.

88
00:05:39.783 --> 00:05:41.527
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:41.827 --> 00:05:53.878
You speak English, don't you? She isn't here, is she? Let's start the lesson, shall we? Each tag matches the auxiliary and changes between positive and negative.

90
00:05:54.178 --> 00:05:56.073
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:56.983 --> 00:06:03.618
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and question tags: positive to negative, negative to positive.

92
00:06:03.918 --> 00:06:08.126
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:06:08.426 --> 00:06:11.194
See you in Unit thirty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:11.494 --> 00:06:14.460
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

